 ref←SetErrorParms ref
⍝ `ref` is typically the result of ##.HandleError.CreateParms.
⍝ Adds Plodder-specific adjustments and returns the ref.
⍝ The crash storm guard is configured in the INI file: `[TRAP]StormGuard` defaults to 1, while
⍝ `[TRAP]StormCeiling` and `[TRAP]StormResetAfter` default to whatever HandleError suggests.
 ref.logFunctionParent←(⍕⎕THIS)
 ref.logFunction←'AppLogError'
 ref.customFns←(⍕⎕THIS),'.SaveCrashRequest'         ⍝ Saves the request the crashed thread was handling.
                                                    ⍝ An application that sets its own must call this one: see the ReadMe
 ref.killThreads←0                                  ⍝ Other threads keep running until `Run` executes ⎕OFF 125,
                                                    ⍝ or for inspection when a Ride is attached
 ref.saveVars←1
 ref.saveErrorWS←0                                  ⍝ Plodder is multi-threaded by design: ⎕SAVE would fail
 :If 0<≢ref.errorFolder←⊃G.INI.Get'TRAP:Folder'
     'CREATE!'F.CheckPath ref.errorFolder
 :EndIf
 ref.stormGuard←1 G.INI.Get'TRAP:StormGuard'
 'Invalid: value of "StormGuard" in INI file'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨~(⊂ref.stormGuard)∊0 1
 ref.stormCeiling←ref.stormCeiling G.INI.Get'TRAP:StormCeiling'
 :If (' '=⊃0⍴∊ref.stormCeiling)∨1≠≢,ref.stormCeiling
 :OrIf (ref.stormCeiling≠⌊ref.stormCeiling)∨1>ref.stormCeiling
     'Invalid: value of "StormCeiling" in INI file'⎕SIGNAL 11
 :EndIf
 ref.stormResetAfter←ref.stormResetAfter G.INI.Get'TRAP:StormResetAfter'
 :If (' '=⊃0⍴∊ref.stormResetAfter)∨1≠≢,ref.stormResetAfter
 :OrIf 0≥ref.stormResetAfter
     'Invalid: value of "StormResetAfter" in INI file'⎕SIGNAL 11
 :EndIf
⍝Done
